1. Definitions
(a) "Software" means ClaudeTool (a Claude desktop pet for Windows), its installer, source code, characters, icons, images, documentation, introduction page, and every file contained in this repository.
(b) "Licensor" means BlackBuddle (GitHub account), named in the copyright notice above.
(c) "Personal User" means an individual (natural person) who uses the Software for himself or herself, without any commercial purpose.
(d) "Plugin" means an extension added to the Software that was made by someone other than the Licensor.

2. Grant
The Licensor grants each Personal User, as long as this license is followed, the right to install and run the Software on his or her own computer and to use it free of charge for personal purposes. This right is non-exclusive, non-transferable, cannot be sublicensed, and may end or be withdrawn under Section 8.

3. What is not allowed
Without the Licensor's prior written permission, you may not:
(a) use the Software for the business or commercial activities of a company, school, organization or institution (use by an individual on his or her own computer as a hobby is not restricted);
(b) sell, rent, lease, host, offer the Software as a service, or include it in another product;
(c) copy, distribute, publish or transmit the Software or any part of it, including modified versions (copying it to install it on your own computer is allowed);
(d) modify the Software or create derivative works (except as permitted by law, and except characters, plugins and settings you create yourself using the Software's own features);
(e) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software to obtain source code (except as permitted by law);
(f) remove or change the copyright notices, trademark notices, or the notices of this license and the disclaimer;
(g) use the Software to harm others or to break the law;
(h) view or fork a public repository within GitHub beyond what GitHub's Terms of Service allow (viewing or forking within that scope is only under GitHub's Terms of Service and does not grant any right not granted by this license).

4. What you create
(a) Characters, plugins and settings you create yourself, and your own questions, answers and data, belong to you; the Licensor claims no rights in them. Characters and plugins made by other people are subject to that person's own terms, and this license does not apply to them.
(b) (Additional permission) The examples provided with the Software (including the guide documents you get with "Get the how-to (.md)" in the app and the example code in them), and plugins made based on those examples, may, notwithstanding Sections 3(c) and 3(d), be copied, modified and given to others, provided that you credit the Licensor as the source by keeping the copyright notice and that you do so for non-commercial purposes. You may also give those guide documents to an AI tool. Commercial use, selling and paid distribution are not covered by this permission and require the Licensor's prior written permission. This permission applies only to the examples and the plugins made from them, and does not change any other provision of this license.

5. Third-party components and trademarks
(a) The Software contains open-source components such as Electron, Chromium and Node.js. Each component remains under its own license; this license does not change them. The list of components and their licenses is in the accompanying THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
(b) "Claude", "Anthropic" and related names and logos are trademarks of Anthropic PBC. This is a personal project and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or approved by Anthropic.

6. Ownership
The copyright and all other rights in the Software belong to the Licensor. This license grants only a right of use and does not transfer ownership. All rights not expressly granted are reserved by the Licensor.

7. No warranty and disclaimer
The Software is provided free of charge "AS IS". Warranties and liability are governed by the accompanying disclaimer (DISCLAIMER.md), which is part of this license.

8. Term and termination
This license begins when you receive the Software. If you breach this license it ends automatically without notice, and you must stop using the Software and delete all copies. The Licensor may withdraw permission for future use at any time. The Software is free, so no refund applies.

9. Other uses
Uses not allowed by Section 3 (business or commercial use, redistribution, etc.) require the Licensor's written permission. Please ask through the GitHub profile of BlackBuddle or the Issues of the introduction-page repository (claude-tool-page). Do not post sensitive information in public.

10. Governing law and jurisdiction
This license is interpreted under the laws of the Republic of Korea, and jurisdiction over disputes follows the Korean Civil Procedure Act.

11. Severability and changes
If any part of this license is invalid or unenforceable, the rest remains in force. The Licensor may change this license; a new version applies from the time it is posted in the repository to Software received or updated after that time.
